ther's electromagnetism. They just happen to travel together in the specific case of "vehicles," which is why the everyday intuition never gets falsified by casual driving experience. So no—"sensing metal mass" isn't a backdoor way of saying "sensing weight." It's sensing a property (conductivity) that has nothing to do with weight in the physics sense, even though in your specific day-to-day sample (cars), the two features are almost always found in the same package.
